        {
          "id": "document_breaking_changes",
          "title": "Document previous_agent_type behavioral change",
          "files": ["dev_artefacts/markdown_docs/parallel-execution.md"],
          "implementation": {
            "add_section": "## Breaking Changes\n\n### previous_agent_type in Parallel Execution\n\n**Behavior Change**: `previous_agent_type` is undefined for agents executing in parallel. This is because there is no single 'previous' agent when multiple agents run concurrently.\n\n**Impact**: Low - most workflows don't rely on this value.\n\n**Mitigation**: Use `agent_idx` for ordering information, or access dependencies directly from `agent_configs`.\n\n**Example**:\n```python\n# Before (sequential)\nagent.previous_agent_type  # Always defined\n\n# After (parallel)\nagent.previous_agent_type  # Undefined for parallel agents\nagent.agent_idx           # Use this for ordering\n```"
          },
          "lines_added": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "add_cli_reference",
          "title": "Document new CLI flags",
          "files": ["dev_artefacts/markdown_docs/parallel-execution.md"],
          "implementation": {
            "add_to_manual_control_section": "#### Control Concurrency\n```bash\nagent-actions run -a my_workflow --concurrency-limit 10\n```\n\nUse this to:\n- Optimize for high-core-count machines (increase limit)\n- Respect API rate limits (decrease limit)\n- Debug resource exhaustion issues"
          },
          "lines_added": 10
        }
      ]
    },

